# =============================================================================
# Local development env — Supabase configuration
# =============================================================================
#
# This project has TWO Supabase projects: staging (default for local dev) and
# production. Local dev should default to staging so destructive ops (test
# bookings, status flips, RLS experiments) don't touch real customer data.
#
# Quick start (new contributor)
# -----------------------------
#   cp .env.example .env            # active env (gitignored, defaults to staging)
#   cp .env.example .env.staging    # preserved staging template
#   npm start                       # reads .env → talks to staging Supabase
#
# Then create your prod template (gitignored) by copying the prod block below
# into a new file `.env.production`.
#
# Switching to prod (rare — prod-bug repro or hotfix verification only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#   cp .env.production .env  &&  restart npm start    # → prod
#   cp .env.staging .env     &&  restart npm start    # → back to staging
#
# Security note
# -------------
# Runtime files (.env, .env.staging, .env.production) are gitignored.
# Only `anon` (publishable, RLS-protected) keys belong in env files.
# NEVER put a `service_role` key in any .env file — it bypasses RLS.
# =============================================================================

